                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="14508797" author="yzhdanov" created="Thu, 23 Apr 2015 10:26:11 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Also consider this &lt;a href=&quot;http://stackoverflow.com/questions/26134208/gridgain-node-disconnect&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://stackoverflow.com/questions/26134208/gridgain-node-disconnect&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14516817" author="yzhdanov" created="Tue, 28 Apr 2015 11:06:05 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Ilya,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I changed several critical discovery timeouts here.&lt;br/&gt;
Please monitor tc in this branch. After it passes please run our common sets of benchmarks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14611908" author="dmagda" created="Thu, 2 Jul 2015 12:52:20 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Yakov, please review. The patch is attached.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14638407" author="dmagda" created="Thu, 23 Jul 2015 07:47:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;So, what has been done by this point:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;introduced failure detection threshold. It is used to detect node failures quickly. There is no need to setup tons of different timeouts and other parameters. Supported for both TcpDiscoverySpi and TcpCommunicationSpi;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;performance optimizations of TcpDiscoverySpi for server nodes: removed heartbeats and status check senders - two Threads;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;introduced connection check message that is sent to the next to check connection aliveness. Connection check frequency is calculated from failure detection threshold automatically;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;connection check message is Externalizable that lets to send the minimal data required across the ring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Yakov, the new patch is available, please review.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14638679" author="dmagda" created="Thu, 23 Jul 2015 11:42:01 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Benchamrked the changes - No drop for ignite-yardstick benchmarks&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14640227" author="dsetrakyan" created="Fri, 24 Jul 2015 09:56:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I looked at the code and have some questions:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;I am not sure &lt;tt&gt;failureDetectionThreshold&lt;/tt&gt; is the right name. Wouldn&apos;t &lt;tt&gt;failureDetectionTimeout&lt;/tt&gt; make more sense?&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;I tried to read the javadoc on &lt;tt&gt;IgniteConfiguration&lt;/tt&gt;, but I think it is trying to say too much. How about this say just briefly explain what it does, without trying to confuse users with explanation of how the implementation works? For example,
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;Failure detection timeout is used to determine how &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;long&lt;/span&gt; a the communication or discovery SPIs should wait before considering a remote connection failed.
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Then in the SPI javadocs for communication and discovery, you can say:
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;{@code failureDetectionTimeout} automatically controls the following parameters: a, b, c, d. If any of those parameters is set explicitly, then the {{failureDetectionTimeout}} setting will be ignored.
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="14640231" author="dsetrakyan" created="Fri, 24 Jul 2015 10:00:06 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;In addition to the above, I think we should print out a warning for cases whenever the &lt;tt&gt;failureDetectionTimeout&lt;/tt&gt; was explicitly set, but we have to ignore it. (disregard this comment, if you are already doing that)&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14640243" author="dmagda" created="Fri, 24 Jul 2015 10:11:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I&apos;m agree to rename &lt;tt&gt;failureDetectionThreshold&lt;/tt&gt; to &lt;tt&gt;failureDetectionTimeout&lt;/tt&gt;, have nothing against this.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also will add 3) to both SPIs javadocs. The same is for 2) - it sounds better and shorter.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14640396" author="dmagda" created="Fri, 24 Jul 2015 12:29:51 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Guys thanks for spending your time on review.&lt;br/&gt;
All your proposed comments are applied.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;TC is green, no performance drop.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Merged the branch into the main development branch.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14640402" author="dmagda" created="Fri, 24 Jul 2015 12:42:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The full list of big changes (excluding minor optimizations and improvements):&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;introduced IgniteConfiguration.failureDetectionTimeout parameter that is used instead of tons of other parameters when it&apos;s required to detect a connection failure between nodes;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;automatic control of bunch of TcpDiscovery and TcpCommunication SPIs parameters when failure detection timeout is set;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;implemented light-weight &quot;ping&quot; message (connection check message) that is sent only to the next node in the topology to check connection status;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;resource usage optimizations: removed two additional threads that were used by every node. One thread was used to send heartbeat messages, the second one used to send status check messages. Now this functionality is a part of message worker thread;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="14645728" author="dmagda" created="Wed, 29 Jul 2015 08:53:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Reopened the ticket because the following changes were applied to the code after benchmarking &apos;node left&apos; case on Amazon EC2:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;connection check message will be sent even if failure detection timeout is not used;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;removed unecessary &lt;tt&gt;pingNode&lt;/tt&gt; call when a remote node fails in &lt;tt&gt;sendMessageAcrossRing&lt;/tt&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;added info on the lowest failure detection timeout in lower-latency networks - 120 ms. Determined with AWS;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Attached:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;new patch (475-2.patch);&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;performance comparision plot that shows how quickly a topology recovers when a node leaves it (failure_detection_timeout_node_left.zip). No drop in compare to the previous results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Yakov, please review one more time.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14649039" author="yzhdanov" created="Fri, 31 Jul 2015 10:29:10 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Changes look good&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14649083" author="dmagda" created="Fri, 31 Jul 2015 11:01:11 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Merged to the master&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
